OL,4,C'Murdered teen's legacy inspired my    
OL,5,Clegal career'                          
OL,6,GA woman who has been supported to      
OL,7,Gtrain as a barrister by a bursary      
OL,8,Gwhich honours a murdered teenager has  
OL,9,Gsaid she wants to become a "hard-      
OL,10,Gworking" prosecutor who "treats        
OL,11,Gwitnesses with care".                  
OL,13,FSharon Uche, 24, from Manchester, said 
OL,14,Fbeing chosen for the Anthony Walker    
OL,15,FBursary Scheme, which supports         
OL,16,Faspiring lawyers from under-           
OL,17,Frepresented backgrounds, had given her 
OL,18,Fthe confidence to "reach my goals" and 
OL,19,F"opened doors".                        
OL,22,                                   G1/4 
