OL,4,CRed plaque honours firefighting war    
OL,5,Cveteran                                
OL,6,GA firefighter who avoided capture      
OL,7,Gduring World War Two by hiding up a    
OL,8,Gtree and later died during fire        
OL,9,Gstation drills has been honoured.      
OL,11,FWilliam McHarry from Workington,       
OL,12,FCumbria, joined Sunderland Fire        
OL,13,FBrigade after serving with the RAF and 
OL,14,Flater became a representative of the   
OL,15,FFire Brigades Union (FBU).             
OL,17,FHe died following a cardiac arrest     
OL,18,Fduring training at Fulwell Fire        
OL,19,FStation in Sunderland on 17 November   
OL,20,F1970, aged 49.                         
OL,22,                                   G4/4 
